  "conversation_id": "8164d318-a055-4d00-beaf-9bc0f70cd542",
  "question": "What are the learning objectives for fractions in Primary 4?",
  "answer": "## Learning Objectives for Fractions in Primary 4 (Mathematics)\n\nThe Primary 4 Mathematics curriculum includes several units that address fractions. Based on the retrieved evidence, the learning objectives are organized by unit as follows:\n\n### Unit C4-U04: Number and Numeration – FRACTION\n- **Identify Equivalent fractions** (C4U04-LO03).\n- **Relate fractions with denominators up to compare equivalent fraction greater than** (C4U04-LO04).\n\n### Unit C4-U05: Number and Numeration – OPERATION ON FRACTIONS\n- **Add Equivalent fractions** (C4U05-LO01).\n- **Subtract Equivalent fractions** (C4U05-LO02).\n- **Solve both Addition and Subtraction of Equivalent fractions** (C4U05-LO03).\n- **Solve word problems involving Addition and Subtraction of Equivalent fractions** (C4U05-LO04).\n\n### Unit C4-U06: Number and Numeration – Operation on Fraction (Multiplication)\n- **Multiply equivalent fractions** (C4U06-LO01).\n- **Multiply like fractions with denominators up to multiply like fractions with denominators up to multiply related fractions with denominators up to multiply related fractions with denominators up to** (C4U06-LO02).\n\n### Unit C4-U07: Number and Numeration\n- **Multiply proper fractions with denominators up to 12** (C4U07-LO01).\n- **Multiply like fractions with denominators up to solve word problems involving proper fractions with denominators up to solve word problems involving proper fractions with denominators up to** (C4U07-LO02).\n\n### Unit C4-U08: Number and Numeration\n- **Order fractions and decimals** (C4U08-LO03).\n\n**Note:** The evidence does not include objectives for comparing fractions beyond equivalent fractions, nor for division of fractions at this grade level. The wording of some objectives (e.g., C4U06-LO02, C4U07-LO02) appears truncated or repetitive in the source records; teachers should refer to the official curriculum document for the complete phrasing.",
  "status": "completed",
